(c)  JP301 states (pin 1 +5V_MOD, pin 2 +5V, pin 3 USB_VBUS_F): one shorting jumper spans two adjacent pins and pin 2 takes one jumper
     no jumper      +5V joined to module: False to cable path: False module joined to cable path: False
     jumper on 1-2  +5V joined to module: True  to cable path: False module joined to cable path: False
     jumper on 2-3  +5V joined to module: False to cable path: True  module joined to cable path: False
(b)  no jumper position joins pin 1 (module) to pin 3 (cable path), checked above for every state; the board never sources current into the cable:
     jumper on 1-2: the cable side (pin 3, USB_VBUS_F) is open at JP301, so nothing from +5V reaches F401, D402 or the cable;
     jumper on 2-3: the module output (pin 1) is open, so the module drives nothing and the cable feeds only the board's own loads;
     with a computer on the cable and the jumper on 1-2 the cable carries only the clamps' leakage (D401 IRM <= 150 nA at 5.25 V, D402 IR <= 400 uA at VR 6.0 V), far under 0.100 A
(d)  jumper on 2-3: capacitance behind the fuse 81.3 uF (C301 and C302 stay on the module's side) against the 10 uF of USB 2.0 7.2.4.1: 8.1x; charge 329 uC
     peak at Rmin 35.0 A (tau 12 us), at R1max 5.25 A (tau 81 us); fuse Imax 100 A; inrush above 8 A lasts about 3 tau = 244 us at most
     undamped step-response bound on the VBUS node: 10.50 V (twice the 5.25 V source); D402 holds it to VC 10.3 V at 19.4 A; with the jumper on 2-3 the fuse output is the +5V rail, so the rail parts (LT1963A input 20 V absolute maximum; U201 and U791 7 V) are exposed to whatever F401 does not damp; no block now sits between them and the cable
     charge through a 44 ohm / 10 uF load: 52 uC; the limit's equivalent is met only with surge limiting ahead of 81.3 uF
(e)  DS4260 2.1 with VBUS open: VCL+ = 31.2 V (6.1 + 0.5 x 24 + 1.1 + 0.5 x 24)
     with VBUS on D402 (Rd 0.151 ohm from its sheet, typical-based): node 9.9 V, VCL+ = 23.0 V; the pin's DC limit is 6 V (4 V with VDD absent)
